These rules apply to every change in this repository. The design source of truth is `docs/site-plan.md` in the project library, and the copy in that file. Do not restyle the site into a generic template.

## Stack

- Next.js App Router. Do not set `output: 'export'`
- TypeScript, `strict`
- Tailwind CSS
- Framer Motion for the fades named in the site plan, and nothing else
- No component library, no CSS-in-JS, no extra animation package
- `next/image` with the default optimizer. Do not set `unoptimized: true`
- Google fonts through `next/font`: Fraunces for display, Outfit for UI and body

## Structure

- Routes: `/` for the home page, `/experience`, `/work`, `/about`, `/photos`, and `/music`. Contact stays on the home page. The nav Contact link is `/#contact`. Nav order is Experience, then Work.
- Content lives in typed modules under `data/`, not in JSX
- Photographs are objects in `data/photos.ts` with `src`, `title`, `alt`, `tags`, `hero`, and `heroPosition`. `hero: false` keeps a portrait of an individual person out of the landing photo. `heroPosition` is the CSS object-position when that photo is the hero. Adding a photo is one new object plus a file in `public/photos/`
- Experience, projects, contact, and music live in `data/content.ts`. A project image is an optional file under `public/projects/`. With no image, the project has no media area. Experience prints for the polaroid stack are `experiencePhotos`, files under `public/experience/`. Arrangements are `arrangements`, each with a YouTube id.
- One component per file under `components/`
- The A logo is an inline SVG component, not an image

## Design constraints

- Paper `#f4f1ec`, ink `#1c1917`, muted `#5c564e`, accent `#9c2f24` only for the mark on paper, text links, the active filter, and the organization name on the experience timeline
- Glass: white at 55% opacity, 20px backdrop blur, 1px white edge, soft shadow
- Card radius 28px, photo radius 20px, filter chips fully rounded
- Content max width 1120px. Hero and photo bands bleed
- No Inter, Roboto, Arial, Space Grotesk, purple gradients, icon-feature grids, skill logo walls, dark-mode toggle, or stock patterns
- Body text never sits on a photograph without glass or a scrim
- Hero photo is chosen at random on each load from gallery photos with `hero: true`, never a portrait flagged off and never the headshot. Do not scale that photo up past its own pixels. Serve the large source.

## Code

- Accessible: real buttons for filters, visible focus, alt text on every photo, contrast that holds on glass
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`
- No phone number in source unless it is explicitly added to `data/content.ts`
- No backend, no contact form, no analytics snippet unless asked
- Do not invent projects, metrics, or employers
- Keep components server-rendered where they can be. The random hero, the home photo preview, and the photo filter are the client pieces
- Match existing names and patterns when you edit. Do not refactor unrelated files

## Hosting

- Vercel’s free tier. No `basePath` and no `assetPrefix`
- The build command is `next build`
- Do not deploy to GitHub Pages
- Do not add a server action, a route handler, or any API unless asked
